gen/mmv1/products/**/*.yaml

  Vendored from GoogleCloudPlatform/magic-modules, at the commit recorded in
  gen/mmv1.lock, by scripts/fetch-schemas.

  Copyright Google Inc. and the magic-modules contributors.
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:
  http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

  Only mmv1/products is vendored, and only its .yaml files. That scope is a
  licence boundary rather than a size one: magic-modules also contains
  mmv1/third_party/ and tools/, which are MPL 2.0 and are NOT redistributed
  here. scripts/fetch-schemas restricts the checkout to mmv1/products and then
  refuses outright if either directory is present, and
  scripts/scripts_test.go's TestFetchSchemasRefusesMPLDirectories keeps that
  refusal honest.

  1127 of the 1132 vendored files carry the Apache 2.0 header inline. The five
  that do not (compute/InstanceTemplate.yaml, dialogflow/Environment.yaml,
  iap/ForwardingRuleRegionalService.yaml, monitoring/Snooze.yaml,
  networkservices/AgentConnectivityTemplate.yaml) omit the boilerplate upstream
  and are covered by the magic-modules repository licence like the rest of the
  tree.

